"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with a meeting on July 15th. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms, with a budget of $2M approved by the executive board. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The project has moved from the design phase to the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, with upcoming UI enhancements planned for October. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Celebrations for milestones are scheduled for October 10th, and team meetings are set for August 1st and August 5th."
